      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BURGUNDY GIRL (3) is the main danger if the class drop from Open company sparks improvement. She had genuine home-turn trouble at Canberra and has an excellent record at this track. Each way. OUR HUNTRESS (4) brings a reliable profile, having placed in nine of 11 starts, but the first look at around 1600m is the key question after she just held third in a Class 2 at Canberra. Worth thought. PEARLER (6) is flying at this venue, winning her past two starts here, and her four-from-four track record keeps her right in the mix despite the rise from BM58 grade. In career-best form and stays in the mix. GOOD PRIZE (2) is experiencing a win drought, extended last start when seventh over 1300m at Canberra after he got a long way back in the run. In the right race and should be about the mark.",
